  "notes": [
    "**Acoger** is an -ER verb with irregular \"yo\" form in present",
    "Present: irregular \"yo\" form (acojo) with spelling change g→j before o",
    "Preterite: regular -ER endings",
    "Imperfect: regular -ER pattern",
    "Future: regular future endings attached to infinitive",
    "Multiple meanings: to welcome, to receive, to host, to shelter",
    "Often used reflexively: **acogerse a** (to take refuge in, to avail oneself of)",
    "Common usage: *acoger a los turistas* (to welcome tourists), *acoger una idea* (to embrace an idea), *acogerse a la ley* (to invoke the law)",
    "Related adjective: **acogedor/acogedora** (welcoming, cozy)"
  ],
